! PITSL [MW/m#3/keV]: Longitudinal ion heat loss in SOL: PITSL=q_i/L, 
!  according to G.Becker, NF, Vol.35, No.1, 35 (1995)
!
! Longitudinal heat flow
! q_i = M n_i 2*T_i v_s = M n_i m_i v_i^2 v_s, M is the Mach number
!   
! v_s = sqrt((T_e+T_i)/m_i)
!
! q_i=9.9e2*M*NI*TI*sqrt(TE+TI)/L, [keV, m -> MW/m^2]
!
! L=0.5*\pi*q_a*R_0
!
!   Usage:  (for implicit scheme)
! PIT=...-PITSL
!   (Pereverzev 15-MAR-99)
PITSL = 9.9e2*0.08*NI(j)*sqrt((TE(j)+TI(j))/AMAIN(j))
! second line added to convert AUG connection length for other machines
! AUG connection length is in factor 0.08
! Mach number is 0.08*L_AUG=0.8
! (G.W.Pacher - 26-03-2001)   *(1.65*4.)/(RTOR/MU(NA1))

